>> Search Chinese polls and you'll find the opposite opinion.
>>
>>
> So do you actually know Chinese?
>

I only asked my Chinese  friends of their opinion on English. This is what
they said on phonology.

Also one must consider extreme politeness of Asian people. They often say
things that won't hurt you. I doubt lo'e Asian can say "I hate
English/Italian" or of any other language.

Thus, I can only consider "hard to pronounce" criterion since "not
aesthetically pleasing" might not be formalizable and measurable.
However, the time one needs to master fluency in phonology can be measured.


